## Instructions
Classify this session using ONLY the structured format below. Do not add prose or explanation.

attack_type: <one of: botnet | credential-spray | targeted | worm | scanner | unknown>
severity: <one of: low | medium | high | critical>
ttps: <comma-separated MITRE ATT&CK technique names or short descriptors, e.g. "brute-force, lateral-movement, dropper-download">

Rules:
- botnet: automated, repeating pattern, typical IoT commands (wget, curl to fixed IPs, busybox)
- credential-spray: login attempts only, few/no commands after success
- targeted: commands suggest reconnaissance of a specific environment (hostname, ifconfig, ps, cat /etc/passwd)
- worm: downloads and re-executes binaries, modifies cron or rc files
- scanner: rapid connect + disconnect, no login success
- critical severity: active dropper download, persistence mechanism, or lateral movement observed
